/-!
# Suggested Lean forms: adic coefficients and the comparison of schemes with v-sheaves

This file is not the roadmap and is not exhaustive. The roadmap document `README.md` is
definitive. These statements suggest Lean forms so that contributors and reviewers converge on
names and signatures. Every proof and every construction of this roadmap is `sorry`; nothing
here is claimed to be formalised.

The schematic layer (compactifications, limits, Nagata) is stated with Mathlib's native
`Scheme`, its morphism properties, its scheme-theoretic image and its cofiltered categories.
The adic spectrum of a Huber pair is Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.spa`.

Objects that other roadmaps own (small v-stacks and v-sheaves, perfectoid spaces, diamonds,
adic spaces, the enhanced derived categories of sheaves and their completion, the discrete
étale categories with their operations, the pro-étale and étale derived categories of schemes)
appear in the section `Interfaces` as opaque *data* stand-ins whose docstrings name the owner;
the owner's definition governs. Only their homotopy categories are visible here: the
presentable stable enhancements, and every statement that needs them, are in the README. The
few predicates used on stand-ins are defined from data (an essential image, a nonempty type of
witnesses, an isomorphism of a unit map); no condition is replaced by a `Prop`-valued
placeholder. Statements about stand-ins speak about the intended objects only.

Target labels such as `L2/compactification` refer to the README.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace TauCeti.AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons

/-! ## Conventions -/

/-- The standing coefficient hypotheses of ECD §26, relative to the characteristic `p` of the
perfectoid test spaces: `Λ` is `I`-adically complete and separated, `I` is generated by a
regular sequence, and `I` contains an integer prime to `p`. For `I = ⊥` (the empty regular
sequence) the last condition says that `Λ` is killed by an integer prime to `p`. -/
structure IsAdicCoefficientPair (p : ℕ) {Λ : Type u} [CommRing Λ] (I : Ideal Λ) : Prop where
  isAdicComplete : IsAdicComplete I Λ
  regular : ∃ rs : List Λ, RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular Λ rs ∧ I = Ideal.ofList rs
  primeToP : ∃ n : ℕ, n.Coprime p ∧ (n : Λ) ∈ I

/-- A discrete coefficient ring killed by an integer prime to `p`, the coefficients of the
finite-level theories. -/
def IsPrimeToPTorsion (p : ℕ) (Λ : Type u) [CommRing Λ] : Prop :=
  ∃ n : ℕ, n.Coprime p ∧ (n : Λ) = 0

/-- The plus ring of the characteristic-`p` scheme avatar: the integral closure of `𝔽_p`
in `R`. -/
abbrev charPPlus (p : ℕ) (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [Algebra (ZMod p) R] : Subring R :=
  (integralClosure (ZMod p) R).toSubring

/-- The base of the mixed-characteristic comparison: a complete discrete valuation ring with its
adic topology and perfect residue field of characteristic `p`. -/
class IsCompleteDVRBase (p : ℕ) (O : Type u) [CommRing O] [IsDomain O]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing O] [TopologicalSpace O] : Prop where
  isAdic : IsAdic (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal O)
  complete : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal O) O
  charP_residue : CharP (IsLocalRing.ResidueField O) p
  perfect_residue : PerfectField (IsLocalRing.ResidueField O)

